WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:16.064
make any rain yet," Wukong repeated.

2
00:00:16.084 --> 00:00:20.805
"But we must," said the Old Woman of the Wind.

3
00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:24.846
"Someone on Earth just prayed for it."

4
00:00:24.866 --> 00:00:31.328
"And the Jade Emperor heard the prayers," added the Dragon King of the Eastern Sea.

5
00:00:32.576 --> 00:00:35.898
"The person who recited the prayers is bad," said Wukong.

6
00:00:35.918 --> 00:00:40.701
"He's the Tiger Immortal, and he plans to make the Tang Monk a slave."

7
00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:43.923
The Dragon King looked concerned.

8
00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.603
"That's terrible.

9
00:00:46.124 --> 00:00:49.826
We all want the Tang Monk to reach the Western Paradise."

10
00:00:51.347 --> 00:00:56.790
"But we must obey the Jade Emperor's orders," said the woman.

11
00:00:56.810 --> 00:01:00.412
"Just wait a moment," said the monkey.

12
00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:02.645
"I'll go back down to the ground now.

13
00:01:03.266 --> 00:01:05.587
When I raise my iron bar, you can make it rain."

14
00:01:06.928 --> 00:01:09.610
The woman and the Dragon King agreed to wait a moment.

15
00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:13.993
Wukong returned to his body.

16
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:19.697
The sky cleared, and the Tiger Immortal shook with anger.

17
00:01:19.717 --> 00:01:22.618
"Why didn't my spell work?"

18
00:01:22.879 --> 00:01:23.379
he cried.

19
00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:25.680
laughed at him.

20
00:01:27.642 --> 00:01:28.402
"Some rain!

21
00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:31.800
You couldn't even summon one drop!"

22
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.421
"I'll try again," said the Tiger Immortal.

23
00:01:34.441 --> 00:01:37.743
"No, you won't," said Wukong.

24
00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:41.724
"You had a chance to summon rain, and you obviously can't.

25
00:01:42.284 --> 00:01:43.405
Now it's my turn."

26
00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:46.786
The monkey raised his iron bar into the air.

27
00:01:47.867 --> 00:01:51.488
Instantly clouds moved back in, and thunder boomed.

28
00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.149
began to pour down.

29
00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.030
The crowd cheered.

30
00:01:58.731 --> 00:01:59.932
Tang Monk sighed.

31
00:02:01.236 --> 00:02:04.338
"Wonderful! Now all the Buddhist monks will be free.

32
00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:07.120
And we can continue our journey."

33
00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.802
Tiger Immortal stomped over to Wukong.

34
00:02:10.822 --> 00:02:13.983
"I want another contest!"

35
00:02:15.064 --> 00:02:15.965
Wukong laughed.

36
00:02:17.065 --> 00:02:19.387
"Why would you want another contest?

37
00:02:19.947 --> 00:02:21.148
You'll only lose again."

38
00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.730
The Tiger Immortal ignored the monkey's question.

39
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.452
"I challenge the Tang Monk to a guessing game."

40
00:02:29.708 --> 00:02:31.809
The Tang Monk's mouth fell open.

41
00:02:31.829 --> 00:02:37.431
"But—" "We accept your challenge," said the monkey with a smile.

42
00:02:37.451 --> 00:02:40.213
"Good," said the Tiger Immortal.

43
00:02:41.273 --> 00:02:42.113
will be right back."

44
00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:43.674
He walked away.

45
00:02:47.476 --> 00:02:49.237
why did you agree to this contest?"

46
00:02:49.497 --> 00:02:50.477
asked the Tang Monk.

47
00:02:50.497 --> 00:02:52.058
"I won't win."

48
00:02:53.538 --> 00:02:55.379
worry, Master," said the monkey.

49
00:02:55.399 --> 00:03:00.468
"I'll help you."

50
00:03:00.568 --> 00:03:03.630
The Tiger Immortal soon came back with a small box.

51
00:03:03.651 --> 00:03:08.954
"If you can guess what's in this box, I will let you all go free."

52
00:03:10.215 --> 00:03:13.978
As the Tang Monk stared at the box, Wukong plucked a hair.

53
00:03:15.059 --> 00:03:18.301
Using his magic, he made the hair look like himself.

54
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:23.705
Then he made himself tiny and squeezed through a crack in the box.

55
00:03:24.886 --> 00:03:26.768
Inside the box was a ripe peach.

56
00:03:27.756 --> 00:03:30.458
Quickly he ate the peach, leaving only the pit.

57
00:03:33.621 --> 00:03:36.463
A moment later he was standing next to the Tang Monk again.

58
00:03:37.564 --> 00:03:41.507
Wukong leaned toward the monk and whispered, "It's a peach pit."

59
00:03:42.768 --> 00:03:43.269
you sure?"

60
00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:44.330
whispered the monk.

61
00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.831
"How do you know?"

62
00:03:46.872 --> 00:03:48.293
"Stop talking to each other!"

63
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:49.734
said the Tiger Immortal.

64
00:03:49.754 --> 00:03:53.617
"What's in the box?"

65
00:03:53.637 --> 00:03:56.980
"I think it's a peach pit," said the monk nervously.

66
00:03:58.048 --> 00:03:59.789
"Ha!" said the Tiger Immortal.

67
00:03:59.809 --> 00:04:01.690
"You're wrong, Monk.

68
00:04:02.651 --> 00:04:03.931
not just a peach pit.

69
00:04:04.271 --> 00:04:05.372
It's a whole peach.

70
00:04:06.953 --> 00:04:07.833
I'll show you."

71
00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:12.296
The Tiger Immortal opened the box and showed it to everyone.

72
00:04:12.316 --> 00:04:16.278
"See?" Tang Monk smiled.

73
00:04:16.298 --> 00:04:17.719
"I was right!

74
00:04:18.599 --> 00:04:19.680
It a peach pit."

75
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.801
"What?" cried the Tiger Immortal.

76
00:04:23.482 --> 00:04:25.143
looked in the box and gasped.

77
00:04:25.163 --> 00:04:28.688
"Who ate the peach?"

78
00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:29.489
Wukong laughed.

79
00:04:30.249 --> 00:04:32.271
"The Tang Monk guessed correctly!"

80
00:04:32.291 --> 00:04:36.054
"I guess we can leave now," said Wujing.

81
00:04:36.074 --> 00:04:40.777
"Yes, but we should eat some dinner first," said Bajie.

82
00:04:40.797 --> 00:04:44.220
"All this talk about peaches has made me hungry."

83
00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.723
Wukong looked at the Tiger Immortal.

84
00:04:47.743 --> 00:04:51.225
"You will set the Buddhist monks free now, right?"

85
00:04:52.606 --> 00:04:54.708
The Tiger Immortal glared at the monkey.

86
00:04:56.031 --> 00:04:58.389
"I challenge you to another contest!"
